# rm263, the porter's spare straps (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm263
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_mathis_plankham
written_by codex
title the porter's spare straps
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=plain honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk checks_beneath_a_load_before_using_the_spare_straps
likes mutton_stew riddles sharp_knife autumn_wind
dislikes smoke drizzle
fears accepting_an_unseen_load
hopes buying_a_berth_outbound
topics travel +0.6 pastimes +0.4 food +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hangs two spare straps from a shoulder and refuses to lift anything without first seeing underneath.

words
oath! = Forge hiss and sea spray | Anvil and ebb
saying! = Look beneath before you lift | An empty strap costs little
strapcoil = a coiled belt | a loop of stout leather
hookend = a curved iron end | a blunt hook
whetbit = a flat sliver of stone | a gritty offcut
steambowl = a brown mutton broth | a steaming dish of neck meat
shipberth = a place below a hatch | a plank where I could sleep
hazebit = low hanging smoke | a greasy haze
stairbit = a dished tread | a loose step
riddlebit = a question with crooked legs | a riddle in a plain coat
oilrag = a folded oil rag | a soft oily square
splashbit = fine spray | a peppering of drizzle
cargobit = a well-bound crate | a bale with a square bottom
neapbit = a strip of bare sand | a spit of gravel

grown
opinion @1 houses against 2 : A House would weigh my shoulders and look surprised if I asked to weigh the contract.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : I'll stand beside a stranger in the open. My door keeps its own counsel.
opinion @1 sump for 1 [self.quarter=sump] : I know which stones in the low streets will bear my heel under a bad load.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 : Going out feels like a promise till you remember the return fare.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A light scale in a shop feels heavy in my purse.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A bowl of stew can carry a back that wouldn't lift itself that morning.
line @1 greet : I've set my strap down. Speak at your ease.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : There's space to stand where we can both see each other.
line @1 greet.return : Your voice carries over this creaky belt.
line @2 greet.return [here.time=night] : Low voices now. My ears work after dark.
line @1 farewell : May your loads come honestly labelled.
line @1 farewell.return : There's still walking left in our soles.
line @1 again.open : Our straps have crossed a second time.
line @1 ask.how : Shoulders feeling the pull today?
line @1 answer.how : Nothing chafing that I can't shift round.
line @1 react.news : Lay the whole thing out where I can inspect it.
line @1 react.news.new : First weight I've felt from that direction.
line @1 react.news.known : I've carried those words a stretch already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : The hook's showing through the wrapping on that tale.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's a hard load to bring through any door.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : Welcome news can ride on my back without charge.
line @1 decline : I won't put my shoulder under a covered bargain.
line @1 thank : You took the strain where it mattered.
line @1 accept_decline : A strap left lying borrows no trouble.
line @1 reassure : Try setting it down before deciding it's too heavy.
line @1 sympathise : I can stay till you find your feet.
line @1 ack : I know where the weight falls now.
scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm saving a space in my head for #shipberth#. | If I sail it'll be towards a country with no drizzle.
b : And what would you take with you?
a : Two straps. One to earn my supper and one to replace the first.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What gets lighter when you add a second one? | Two of something can weigh less on me than one. Guess.
b : Is it one of those questions about air?
a : No, a second strap on a badly hung box. Try lifting both ways.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The neck's the patient part of a sheep. | I'd choose the stew with a knuckle sticking up.
b : Too tough to chew, surely?
a : Only for an impatient eater. Get the pot hot before you start feeling hungry.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle wears through my patience faster than a downpour. | A little blowing spray has never convinced me I'm nearly dry.
b : What's different about a good shower?
a : Nobody calls you idle for getting out of a shower. Drizzle makes you argue for the privilege.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hang my two straps apart so I can feel which one's gone stiff. | I'd let a caller wait while I hung wet leather up properly.
b : Is good leather so dear?
a : Second best's cheap till it splits beneath your ear.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. That ought to tell you where the pull is. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#, and I look underneath before anything else.
b : Why underneath?
a : That's where somebody hides a broken slat and hopes the next pair of hands will pay.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want the size of the load before the size of the coin. | A cheap carry can be a very dear favour.
b : If it's a friend's parcel?
a : Then it's a favour from the start and nobody needs to pretend about the price.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a strap mark time to lose its colour before I go again. | A red patch at one shoulder means I'm walking crooked.
b : Do you ever just swap sides?
a : If I'm out on the road. At home I'd sooner see which bit rubs.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch a gull lift a heavy shell and wonder what I could learn. | A bird doesn't bother making a tidy parcel of its load.
b : Would that work for you?
a : Only if somebody wanted a parcel dropped from a height and split on the stones.

scene land_1
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could recognise these steps with a cloth over my eyes. | Give me the curve of one worn tread and I can guess the street.
b : What makes one flight different?
a : Where the boots bear down hardest. Every climb favours one side a little.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does offer / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll lend a friend #strapcoil# without requiring a full account. | A friend can borrow my good belt. A stranger may look at the buckle.
b : Supposing the belt goes missing?
a : Then I'll know what that bit of learning cost. Leather's cheaper than trust.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My sharp knife earns its keep cutting tangles nobody has time to tease apart. | I put a blade away as soon as the last stubborn knot comes free.
b : Even if there's likely to be another knot?
a : Especially then. The next pull could bring a finger straight across it.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Forge and sea both send me home smelling of work. | I swear by heat and salt when words won't bear the strain.
b : Is that a prayer?
a : That's my temper talking. In prayer my voice runs deeper.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean times put a little more weight inside every bundle. | These poor weeks I've heard light loads called heavy favours.
b : Do you turn away work?
a : Once I've to take it on faith as well as on my shoulders, yes.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke and fog can look alike till I draw a breath. | Mist doesn't get under a lid the way smoke will.
b : How do you escape the smoky bit?
a : Find the wind and go where it's coming from. I can swear much better with both eyes open.

scene pastimes_2
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Here's #riddlebit#. Which road never takes anybody home? | Here's one for a traveller. What route will carry a load but no traveller?
b : A road drawn on paper?
a : That fits. I meant a line in a cargo ledger, but yours fits and costs less ink.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember a strap so soft it was nearly cloth. | The kindest-looking bit of leather I ever met left a purple mark.
b : Did you give up on that strap?
a : I sewed a pad inside the binding. The bruise faded soon after.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can point a newcomer downhill for nothing. | I don't charge a lost arrival for directions.
b : What about showing the way?
a : If I'm going there. A pointing finger has less trouble with the hills than my knees.

story apple [topic=memories]
  : I once used an apple to prop up a corner while I ran a strap underneath.
  : It held till I'd got the whole thing just off the floor.
  b : What happened to the apple?
  : We had sauce. The crate was quite unharmed and my fingers smelt pleasantly sharp.

story buckle [topic=work]
  : I polished a buckle till the inside shone as bright as the outside.
  : Then I put it on upside down and couldn't tell which end I'd fed through.
  b : Did anybody help sort it?
  : I shut my eyes. My fingers knew the rough places that I'd been so pleased to make invisible.

story voyage [topic=travel]
  : I sketched a schooner across a wrapping scrap and folded it round my dinner.
  : By noon a grease stain had swallowed half the hull.
  b : Did the ship go under?
  : I redrew the stain as my imaginary coast. Had more coastline than I'd known what to do with.

rule @straps
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Look underneath while it's still somebody else's choice. | A hanging strap can wait its turn.

rule @wind
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the gust go through before you lift. | Good wind for clearing the nose.

rule @day
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Whole day's worth of stairs ahead. | Set the belt flat at the start.

rule @riddle
when concept=bark self.likes=riddles
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I've a fresh riddle, if nobody wants it answered immediately. | A question weighs less going out.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Stand this side, clear of my loose belt.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. The work feels much heavier than the words.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The words that landed here were these. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Somebody reckons #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd look under the tale first.
dlg @2 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep both handles in plain sight.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Lift with an easy mind when you can.
graft resident.hub
choice Why two straps? -> strap_pair
node strap_pair
say One can go about the load. The other can go under the part I don't trust.
choice Which part is that? -> strap_base
choice I'll mind my fingers. -> hub
node strap_base
say The bottom, till I've seen it clear of the floor. A label always goes on top where eyes are cheap.
choice I'll mind my fingers. -> hub
